  "start_urls_note": "start_urls[0] is the archive root (its 'Issues' dropdown enumerates every issue page). start_urls[1:] are all 162 issue pages, enumerated explicitly on 2026-08-29 so a pager bug cannot silently truncate collection to one listing page.",
  "source": "claude_code_skill",
  "metadata": {
    "journal_name": "Fordham Law Review",
    "platform": "WordPress",
    "url": "https://fordhamlawreview.org/",
    "created_date": "2026-08-29",
    "status": "superseded_duplicate",
    "navigation": {
      "archive_root": "https://fordhamlawreview.org/law-review/current-issue/",
      "volume_url_pattern": "https://fordhamlawreview.org/issuescategory/{month}-{year}-vol-{N}-no-{M}/",
      "archive_path": "homepage -> Issues (/law-review/current-issue/) -> issue dropdown lists all /issuescategory/ pages -> issue page lists /issues/{slug}/ article pages -> article page links the PDF under /wp-content/uploads/{YYYY}/{MM}/*.pdf",
      "pagination": "none-at-archive-level (full issue list is in the archive root's dropdown); issue pages are server-rendered in full (largest issue, april-2002-vol-70-no-5, renders all 35 articles with no pager)",
      "pagination_url_template": null,
      "pagination_verified": "Archive root yields 162 distinct /issuescategory/ URLs covering volumes 68-94 with no gaps. WP REST /wp-json/wp/v2/issuescategory reports 164 terms but its ?page= paging is broken (repeats rows), so REST must NOT be used to enumerate; the HTML dropdown is authoritative. JetEngine load-more exists in markup but is not needed for issue pages.",
      "total_volumes_estimated": 27,
      "total_issues": 162,
      "total_articles_estimated": 2366,
      "article_count_source": "X-WP-Total on /wp-json/wp/v2/issues?per_page=1 = 2366",
      "pdf_location": "article-detail-page",
      "needs_headless": false,
      "robots": "https://fordhamlawreview.org/robots.txt: Disallow /wp-admin/ (Allow admin-ajax.php) and Disallow /wp-content/uploads/vj-wp-import-export/. No Crawl-delay. Article PDFs under /wp-content/uploads/{YYYY}/{MM}/ are permitted. Sitemap line points at /sitemap_index.xml but that URL 404s.",
      "notes": "Elementor + JetEngine WordPress. Requires a full browser User-Agent: short UAs get HTTP 406 from the origin WAF on /wp-json/ paths. PDF coverage is partial in older volumes -- confirmed PDFs back to 2014 (vol 82), but some pre-2019 entries are metadata stubs with no PDF and no body text (e.g. all of vol 68, 1999). Volumes 1-67 (1914-1998) are not on this site at all; the complete back-run lives on Digital Commons at ir.lawnet.fordham.edu/flr (seed fordham_law_review.json). Issue-page cards carry title + author only, so volume/issue/year must be parsed from the issue page URL slug (vol-{N}-no-{M}) or from the PDF; the article detail page also shows 'Vol. N'/'No. M' headings but only as unclassed Elementor headings. Fordham Law Review Online (/fordham-law-review-online/) is a separate JetEngine listing with a JS load-more and is NOT covered by this seed. Author cards link each byline separately, so the seed uses div.a-author a:nth-of-type(1..5) (SelectorDrivenAdapter returns only the first match per selector, and ids containing 'author' are accumulated); a whole-heading fallback was deliberately omitted because it would re-add a 'By ...' string as an author; this keeps co-authors instead of dropping them."
    },
    "status_reason": "SUPERSEDED 2026-08-30: Fordham Law Review is already collected from its Digital Commons mirror (3,241 dc-flr-*.pdf under corpus/scraped/ir.lawnet.fordham.edu, seed fordham_law_review.json). This WordPress source is the same journal under different filenames, so no filename-level check would catch the overlap. Retain only if the WordPress site is later shown to carry volumes the DC mirror lacks.",
    "smoke_test": {
      "date": "2026-08-29",
